t.card(p,'03 02 05','Define exchange rate (2). Identify two functions of money (2). Explain one commercial-bank function (2). Identify two role differences between a central bank and a commercial bank (2).','An exchange rate prices one currency in another. Money is a medium of exchange and unit of account. A commercial bank provides a payment account so customers can receive and transfer funds. Central banks perform system-level monetary functions, while commercial banks provide customer deposit/credit services; monetary policy is distinct from assessing an individual customer loan.',['Meaning (2): one currency’s price/value (1), expressed in another (1). Separate points for functions (2): medium of exchange (1), unit of account (1). Explanation (2): payment account service (1), enables receipt/transfers (1). Distinct role contrasts (2): system-level versus customer services (1), monetary policy versus individual loan assessment (1). Marks allocation 8.'])
